          "id": 1067070337,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The test failures should be fixed now.\n\nI noticed that ntp.precision used to be signed for most of the wireshark history, but it was changed to uint8 in commit 77b4b938e30c4e2fd8cb100cb018c0f7506ad06a. There is no explanation in the message and https://code.wireshark.org/review/29178 no longer exists.\n\nI'm not sure what advantages it had as unsigned. I think people writing filters using the precision or poll value would want to write it directly as signed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 1832607,
            "username": "mlichvar",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Miroslav Lichvar",
            "state": "active",
